<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#ChangeLog">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A log of changes made to the system during its lifecycle.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AIProvider">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body that develops an AI system or a general-purpose AI model or that has an AI system or a general-purpose AI model developed and places it on the market or puts the AI system into service under its own name or trademark, whether for payment or free of charge.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasHumanOversight">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI system to a mechanism for human oversight or intervention.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DataProcessing">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of combining, preprocessing data resulting in a different dataset.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#isStoredAt">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI artifact to the location or entity where it is stored.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#ExplorationAndValidation">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of reviewing data requirements, sources, and initial assessments.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#annotationTool">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Tool or platform used to perform annotation (e.g., internal tool, external labeling platform).</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#ComputationalResource">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A computational resource used during the AI lifecycle, such as GPUs, CPUs, clusters or cloud instances.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AIDeployer">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Any natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body using an AI system under its authority except where the AI system is used in the course of a personal non-professional activity</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasRisk">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI artifact (e.g., model or dataset) or an AI system to an associated risk. An AI risk can be modelled using the AIRO ontology. Risk means the combination of the probability of an occurrence of harm and the severity of that harm.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DataTesting">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of using datasets for model testing. Testing data means data used for providing an independent evaluation of the AI system in order to confirm the expected performance of that system before its placing on the market or putting into service.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#VisualDocumentation">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Visual documentation of an AI system including photographs, illustrations, diagrams, or renderings that show external features, internal layout, or markings as required by Annex IV.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#labelingGuideline">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Guidelines or instructions provided to annotators when assigning labels.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#Deployment">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of delivering the AI system to production environments.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasAIActivity">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI Lifecycle Phase to a specific AI Activity.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DataTraining">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of using datasets for model training. Training data means data used for training an AI system through fitting its learnable parameters.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AIAgent">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A superclass for all agents involved in the AI lifecycle, derived from prov:Agent.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#storesLogsAt">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a monitoring activity to where its logs are stored.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#providesComputationalResource">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a hardware component to the computational resource it provides.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#affects">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an activity to the artifact it affects or modifies.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasSourceDataset">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a DataProcessing activity to its source datasets.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DeclarationOfConformity">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A document declaring the system's conformity with standards, such as the EU Declaration of Conformity.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#startDate">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The start date of the change.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasVisualDocumentation">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI system to visual documentation such as photographs, diagrams, or illustrations showing external features, markings, and internal layout.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#TransparencyMeasure">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A feature or measure to ensure the transparency of an AI system.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#MLPipeline">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The pipeline for machine learning-centric activities in the AI lifecycle.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#LabelingProcedure">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">An activity describing how data labels were assigned, including annotators, tools and guidelines.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DataSheet">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Structured documentation for a dataset or training configuration, including provenance, scope and main characteristics.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#SoftwareComponent">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A logical or physical software component of the AI system, such as a service, module, or microservice participating in the overall processing.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#Dataset">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Represents a dataset used in the AI lifecycle.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DataPipeline">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The pipeline for data-centric activities in the AI lifecycle.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasTransparencyMeasure">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI system to measures in place to ensure transparency.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#ChangeRecord">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A record of a change, including reason, start and end date, stakeholders, and the change itself.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DataMonitoringAndLogging">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of capturing system events, performance, and traceability.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#evaluationMethod">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The methodology used to evaluate a performance metric.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#reasonForChange">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The reason for the change.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#resourceConfiguration">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Configuration details of the computational resource (e.g., number and type of GPUs, CPU cores, memory, accelerator type).</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#isProvidedBy">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI system to its provider.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#resourceVendor">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Provider or vendor of the computational resource (e.g., cloud provider, hardware manufacturer).</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#implementsTask">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AIMethod to the AITask it is designed to perform.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasInterface">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI system to the interface it provides to users or operators.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#resourceType">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Type of computational resource used (e.g., GPU cluster, CPU server, cloud instance).</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#recordsChange">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links the change record to the change (airo:Change).</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#isDeployedBy">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI system to its deployer.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasFrequency">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Specifies the frequency or recurrence pattern at which an AI activity is performed.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#ModelEngineering">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of defining architecture, selecting algorithms, and training the model.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#SoftwareImplementation">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Represents the concrete, executable software that realizes an algorithm.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#usesValidationData">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a validation activity to the dataset used for validation.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#ExplainableAIFeature">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A specific feature designed to provide explanations for the AI system's output.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasComponent">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AISystem to its constituent components like models and datasets.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasStakeholder">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links the change record to stakeholders (airo:stakeholder or aidoc-ap:AIAgent).</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AIArtifact">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A superclass for all tangible inputs and outputs of the AI lifecycle, derived from prov:Entity for provenance tracking.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasPerformanceMetric">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an evaluation activity to the performance metric it uses.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AIActivity">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A superclass for all activities in the AI lifecycle, derived from prov:Activity.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#modality">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The physical form or modality in which the AI system is provided (e.g., standalone software, API).</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#usesTrainingData">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a training activity to the dataset used for training.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#stores">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a storage location or entity to the AI artifacts it stores.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DataWrangling">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of ensuring data quality through cleaning, filtering, and enrichment.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#ModelVersioning">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of managing revisions and tracking changes in model iterations.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#usesAIMethod">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI model to the specific AI method it is based on.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasDeclarationOfConformity">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI system to its EU Declaration of Conformity document.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#dependsOn">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a system or component to its software.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DataCleaningProcedure">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A procedure describing how data cleaning is performed, such as outlier detection and removal of invalid records.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#requiresHardware">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a system or artifact to the hardware components or servers it needs to run.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#dataScope">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Project-specific summary of the scope of the data contained in the dataset (e.g., population, geography, time period). For interoperable modeling, more specific aspects SHOULD be captured using dcterms:spatial, dcterms:temporal and dcterms:coverage.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#qualityMetricsUsed">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Data quality metrics or thresholds used to assess the dataset after cleaning.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#PostMarketPerformanceEvaluationActivity">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of evaluating system performance in the post-market phase.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#appliesStandard">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI system to a standard it has applied for compliance.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#PerformanceMetric">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A metric used to evaluate the performance of an AI system.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#feedsIntoComponent">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Indicates that the output of one software component is used as input by another, forming part of the system's processing flow.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#supportsCapability">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Indicates that an AITask contributes to achieving a broader AISystemCapability.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AIMethod">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Reflects a mathematical algorithm which computes input data to execute an AI task.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#Log">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A record of system events, performance, and traceability.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AISystem">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">An AI system is a machine-based system that is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy and that may exhibit adaptiveness after deployment, and that, for explicit or implicit objectives, infers, from the input it receives, how to generate outputs such as predictions, content, recommendations, or decisions that can influence physical or virtual environments.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#Auditor">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">An organization or person responsible for reviewing the AI system for compliance.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#outlierHandlingMethod">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Methods used to identify and handle outliers or other problematic records in the data.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AIMethodCategory">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A conceptual grouping of AI methods based on shared characteristics, such as machine learning, search optimization, or knowledge representation.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#HumanOversightMechanism">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A mechanism or measure to facilitate human intervention or supervision.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DataValidation">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of using datasets for model validation. Validation data means data used for providing an evaluation of the trained AI system and for tuning its non-learnable parameters and its learning process in order, inter alia, to prevent underfitting or overfitting.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AITask">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">An action to achieve a specific goal using an AI model.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#ModelPackaging">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of preparing the trained model for deployment.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasArchitecture">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a system or model to a description of its architecture.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#SoftwareCodePipeline">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The pipeline for software development-centric activities in the AI lifecycle.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasLifecycleStage">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI system to its various phases throughout its entire lifecycle.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#annotatorType">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Type of annotators involved in the labeling procedure (e.g., domain experts, laypersons, crowd workers).</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasResponsibleDeveloper">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a software development activity to the developers responsible for it.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#ModelEvaluation">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of assessing performance, robustness, and accuracy.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#version">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The version of the AI system or artifact.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#DataAcquisitionActivity">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The activity of obtaining data from various sources.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasChangeRecord">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a ChangeLog to one or more ChangeRecords.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#Decommissioning">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of taking a model out of production.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#endDate">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The end date of the change.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#dataSelectionCriteria">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Project-specific description of inclusion and exclusion criteria or sampling strategy used to select data for the dataset. Related sampling and bias information MAY also be represented using dqv:hasQualityAnnotation on the dataset or a dedicated sampling-plan resource.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#BuildAndIntegrationTesting">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of building system components and conducting integration testing.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#depicts">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Description of what the visual documentation shows (e.g., 'external view', 'internal layout', 'marking placement').</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#Standard">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A harmonised or other standard applied to the AI system.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#intendedPurpose">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Intended purpose means the use for which an AI system is intended by the provider, including the specific context and conditions of use, as specified in the information supplied by the provider in the instructions for use, promotional or sales materials and statements, as well as in the technical documentation.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#TrainingDataSheet">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A data sheet focusing on training methodologies, techniques, hyperparameters and dataset usage for training, validation and testing.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#HardwareComponent">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Represents the hardware required for an AI system to run.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AISystemCapability">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Represents a category of tasks or functions that an AI system can perform, such as sensory, knowledge, or control action processing.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#SoftwareDependency">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A software package or library that the AI system depends on.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#SoftwareVersioning">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of managing revisions and tracking changes in software iterations.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#producesDataset">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a DataProcessing activity to the finished dataset it produces.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#usesTestData">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a testing activity to the dataset used for testing.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#PostMarketMonitoringActivity">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of monitoring the system's performance and behavior after deployment.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#dataCollectionMethod">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Project-specific description of the method used to collect the data (e.g., manual annotation, web scraping, sensor logs). For interoperability, this SHOULD be complemented with dcterms:provenance and, where appropriate, schema:measurementTechnique.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasSoftwareComponent">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links an AI system to its software components, such as services or modules that participate in the overall processing.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#dataCharacteristic">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Project-specific summary of key characteristics of the dataset, such as feature types, label distributions, data modalities or known biases. For interoperable descriptions, individual variables SHOULD be modeled with schema:variableMeasured and quality aspects with dqv:hasQualityMeasurement / dqv:hasQualityAnnotation.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#hasCapability">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#">Relates an AISystem to an AISystemCapability it is designed to exhibit or support</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#missingDataStrategy">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Strategy for handling missing data (e.g., imputation, deletion, flagging).</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#Interface">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">The interface provided for users or operators of an AI system.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#SoftwareDevelopment">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Activity of developing and writing software code for the AI system.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AIResearcher">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A person involved in the technical development of an AI system.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#AIModel">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">A computational representation that enables an AI method to execute an AI task.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap#logsActivity">
	<comment xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xml:lang="en">Links a monitoring activity to the type of activity that is logged.</comment>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap/data/6df45f1d8587455181836b1820d0507b/e4366486-7226-4673-a6b8-4c30fecf102c">
	<contentSize xmlns="https://schema.org/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0</contentSize>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap/data/11c2616706094c729de4281577d08838/915dc2e0-9070-4db1-baf6-0dec335d7031">
	<contentSize xmlns="https://schema.org/" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">0</contentSize>
</rdf:Description>

<rdf:Description rdf:about="https://w3id.org/aidoc-ap/data/348516cbcb884f1f916e4cdacfcab2f5/0f9e8937-ceb0-4b29-b873-b8f3b1e4f577">
